 "answer": "**Yes—Singapore’s haze has been bad.** NEA’s latest regional update, at **6:25 p.m. on October 17**, reported air quality at **Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy** levels. It is now early **October 18** in Singapore, and I can’t confirm whether conditions have improved overnight. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/corporate-functions/weather/regional-haze-situation))\n\nIf you’re heading out, check the **1-hour PM2.5 reading for your area** on NEA’s haze site or myENV app. NEA recommends that reading for decisions about activity in the next hour; if it’s *High*, avoid strenuous outdoor activity. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
